A library component with a body renders it.

`sngl:ui/markup`'s `list` is a `vbox` with an indent and `listItem` is a row
with a marker column, both written in SNGL -- which is the point of writing
them there: a target implements the primitives and inherits the blocks. html
overrides both with `<ul>` and `<li>`, the element it has for a list, so the
html half here is that override and bubbletea is the library body. Until the two changes this fixture pins,
neither body reached a backend at all. The loader checked a component body
only for the target tiers, so every other tier's converted to an empty one,
and the inliner declined to splice a component it did not declare, so the node
survived to codegen carrying a body no backend reads. Both together meant
`list { listItem { … } }` emitted its children and none of the layout around
them, silently, on every target.

The bullet is the second assertion and it comes from the first: `listItem`
asks `listDepth` for it, `list` provides one more than it was given, and the
nested list therefore draws a different bullet from the one it sits in -- a
body reading a context through a slot, which only works because the body is
there to read it. On html the browser picks a nested `<ul>`'s bullet, and none
is drawn as text.

On bubbletea the bullet is a ternary Go cannot write, hoisted to `__ltN` and
folded once the item is inlined. The fold left a bare assignment, which a view
body draws nothing for, so the bullet rendered as the temp's zero.

deny * `\blistDepth\b` -- the context name is not a symbol any target declares
deny out/none/html/index.html `<span>[•◦▪]</span>` -- html's list is a <ul>, whose bullets are the browser's, not a span of text
deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `var __lt\d+ string\n` -- a hoisted ternary temp is declared with its value, not assigned after
-- doc.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"
import md "sngl:ui/markup"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
    go {
        bubbletea
    }
}

ui.window #home(title="list") {
    md.list {
        md.listItem {
            ui.text(value="one")
        }
        md.listItem {
            md.list {
                md.listItem {
                    ui.text(value="nested")
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
